\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Changing the representation or changing the background}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The equality in \ref{fdip-00UN} keeps the link assignment
#{U} fixed and replaces #{\rho} by its algebraic dual.
By contrast, charge conjugation in the pure-#{SU(N)}
transfer model of \ref{fdip-00NC} changes the background by
#{U\mapsto\overline U}. That result uses the group
automorphism, its action on Haar probability, the admitted
central kernel and an invariant potential.}

\p{For a general finite group, an automorphism whose pullback
realizes the dual representation is extra data. A symmetry of
the [coupled finite sum](fdip-00TU) induced by such a background
map also requires its weight to be invariant. Neither this
background symmetry nor a chosen fiber self-duality follows
from equality of two determinant values.}
